IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mai-dates`
IMPORT `mai-core`
IMPORT `mai-seat`

-- Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 (Qld) -- cases from the seat of the claimant.
--
-- Every expected value is worked by hand from the deposited text (act-1994-009, current on 22 September 2026), with
-- the arithmetic in the comment above it. Every person and figure here is HYPOTHETICAL, including the Minister's offer
-- limits under s 100A (not deposited) and each period of limitation (Limitation of Actions Act 1974, not deposited).
--
-- A breached DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable l4, so regulative rules are asserted where the trace ends
-- FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it does not. Clock: days. A deadline is noticed only at a
-- later event, so a trace that lets a period run out without the claimant acting uses an event by another party.
--
-- Readings used (mai-dates.l4): "within 1 month after" a day ends on the same day next month, or the last day of a
-- shorter month; "within 14 days after" ends 14 days later; "at least 7 days before" ends 7 days before.

`d` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- Date helpers.
-- =====================================================================================================================
-- 31 January + 1 month: February has no 31st, so 28 February 2025 and (leap year) 29 February 2024.
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `months after` (`d` 31 1 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `the day` 1 `months after` (`d` 31 1 2024) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2024
-- 15 November + 3 months crosses the year: 15 February 2026.
#ASSERT `the day` 3 `months after` (`d` 15 11 2025) EQUALS `d` 15 2 2026
#ASSERT `the day` 7 `days before` (`d` 3 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 24 2 2026

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 1. Sam, an adult, is hit by an insured car in Brisbane on 10 March 2025. Symptoms are immediate. He first
-- consults a lawyer about a claim on 20 May 2025.
-- =====================================================================================================================
-- s 4: an incident giving rise to a liability covered by the scheme; Sam, the injured person, claims damages.
#ASSERT `Am I a claimant` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the injured person` EQUALS `yes, I am a claimant`
#ASSERT `Am I a claimant` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a person acting for the injured person in a representative capacity` EQUALS `yes, I am a claimant`
#ASSERT `Am I a claimant` TRUE TRUE TRUE `a dependant of an injured person who died of the injury` EQUALS `yes, I am a claimant`
-- Not covered by the statutory insurance scheme: no motor vehicle accident, so no claim ("means").
#ASSERT `Am I a claimant` TRUE FALSE TRUE `the injured person` EQUALS `no: there is no claim for damages for personal injury from a motor vehicle accident`
#ASSERT `Am I a claimant` TRUE TRUE FALSE `the injured person` EQUALS `no: there is no claim for damages for personal injury from a motor vehicle accident`
-- Someone else: the definition of claim "includes" the fatal-injury claims without closing the list.
#ASSERT `Am I a claimant` TRUE TRUE TRUE `someone else` EQUALS `the Act's definition does not settle it for someone in my position`

-- s 31(1)(a): an insured, identified vehicle with an identified, solvent insurer: the CTP insurer.
#ASSERT `Whom do I claim against` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the insurer is` `the insurer under the vehicle's CTP insurance policy`
-- s 33(3) limits only the Nominal Defendant: a CTP insurer is still the insurer for an accident outside Queensland.
#ASSERT `Whom do I claim against` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the insurer is` `the insurer under the vehicle's CTP insurance policy`
-- s 31(1)(b): uninsured, owned by a self-insurer.
#ASSERT `Whom do I claim against` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the insurer is` `the self-insurer that is the vehicle's registered owner`
-- s 31(1)(c): uninsured, not a self-insurer: the Nominal Defendant.
#ASSERT `Whom do I claim against` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the insurer is` `the Nominal Defendant`
-- s 31(1)(d): the vehicle, or its CTP insurer, cannot be identified.
#ASSERT `Whom do I claim against` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the insurer is` `the Nominal Defendant`
#ASSERT `Whom do I claim against` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the insurer is` `the Nominal Defendant`
-- s 33(3): an unidentified vehicle outside Queensland: the Nominal Defendant is not liable; but it is if gratuitously
-- insured under s 23(7), or where the liability arises from an insolvent insurer under s 33(2).
#ASSERT `Whom do I claim against` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Nominal Defendant is not liable for this accident outside Queensland (s 33(3))`
#ASSERT `Whom do I claim against` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the insurer is` `the Nominal Defendant`
#ASSERT `Whom do I claim against` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the insurer is` `the Nominal Defendant`

-- s 34: particulars given to police under TORUM s 93(4) are appropriate notice; if not, the s 34 form is needed.
#ASSERT `Must I tell the police` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `appropriate notice has been given: the particulars required under the Transport Operations (Road Use Management) Act 1995 s 93(4) were given`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the police` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the claimant must ensure a police officer is given notice under s 34, in the form approved by the commission`
#ASSERT `Must I tell the police` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no duty under s 34: no claim is proposed`

-- s 37(2)(b): 9 months after 10 March 2025 is 10 December 2025; 1 month after 20 May 2025 is 20 June 2025; the
-- earlier is 20 June 2025. Not given, asked 1 June and on the last day: due by 20 June 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE TRUE (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 20 5 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 6 2025) EQUALS `notice of the claim must be given by` (`d` 20 6 2025)
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE TRUE (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 20 5 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 20 6 2025) EQUALS `notice of the claim must be given by` (`d` 20 6 2025)
-- Asked on 21 June 2025, not given: late; it must still be given, with a reasonable excuse (s 37(3)).
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE TRUE (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 20 5 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 21 6 2025) EQUALS `notice is late: it must still be given, with a reasonable excuse for the delay (s 37(3))` (`d` 20 6 2025)
-- Given on 20 June 2025: in time. Given on 21 June 2025: late.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE TRUE (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 20 5 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 20 6 2025) (`d` 1 7 2025) EQUALS `notice was given within the s 37(2) period`
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE TRUE (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 20 5 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 21 6 2025) (`d` 1 7 2025) EQUALS `notice is late: it must still be given, with a reasonable excuse for the delay (s 37(3))` (`d` 20 6 2025)
-- No lawyer consulted: 9 months, 10 December 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE TRUE (`d` 10 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 6 2025) EQUALS `notice of the claim must be given by` (`d` 10 12 2025)
-- Symptoms first appeared 1 April 2025, no lawyer: 9 months after the symptoms, 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 4 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 6 2025) EQUALS `notice of the claim must be given by` (`d` 1 1 2026)
-- A lawyer first consulted on 31 May 2025: 1 month is 30 June 2025 (June has no 31st), earlier than 10 December.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE TRUE (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 31 5 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 6 2025) EQUALS `notice of the claim must be given by` (`d` 30 6 2025)
-- A lawyer first consulted after the 9 months would end (1 December 2025, so 1 January 2026): the 9 months win.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE TRUE (`d` 10 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 12 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 6 2025) EQUALS `notice of the claim must be given by` (`d` 10 12 2025)

-- The s 37 rule for Sam. Day 0 is 10 March 2025; 20 June 2025 is 21 (rest of March) + 30 + 31 + 20 = day 102.
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 10 3 2025) `to` (`d` 20 6 2025) EQUALS 102
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 37 -- the claimant must give notice of the claim within the period, and after it with a reasonable excuse` 102 TRUE 0) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `give notice of the claim` 102)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Late: the period passes (an insurer's event on day 103 marks it), and the continuing obligation is met with a
-- reasonable excuse on day 150. For an identified vehicle there is no bar.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 37 -- the claimant must give notice of the claim within the period, and after it with a reasonable excuse` 102 TRUE 0) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `give written notice responding to the notice of claim` 103), (EVENT `the claimant` `give notice of the claim with a reasonable excuse for the delay` 150)) EQUALS FULFILLED

-- s 37AA: the law practice he first retained gave no s 36A certificate; because of that he could not give notice in
-- time, and he ended the engagement in writing on 25 June 2025: refund by 9 July 2025 (25 June + 14).
#ASSERT `Must my law practice refund my fees` TRUE TRUE TRUE (`d` 25 6 2025) EQUALS `the supervising principal must refund all fees and costs, including disbursements, by` (`d` 9 7 2025)
#ASSERT `Must my law practice refund my fees` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 25 6 2025) EQUALS `s 37AA gives no refund on these facts`
#ASSERT `Must my law practice refund my fees` TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 25 6 2025) EQUALS `s 37AA gives no refund on these facts`
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 37AA -- the supervising principal must refund all fees and costs within 14 days after the termination` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the supervising principal` `refund all fees and costs` 14)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the supervising principal, "s 37AA(2): fees and costs ... were not refunded within 14 days after the termination" (refund on day 15)
#TRACE `s 37AA -- the supervising principal must refund all fees and costs within 14 days after the termination` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the supervising principal` DOES `refund all fees and costs` AT 15

-- s 39: the insurer received his notice on 2 July 2025; it must respond by 16 July 2025 (2 + 14).
#ASSERT `Is the insurer taken to accept my notice` (`d` 2 7 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 16 7 2025) EQUALS `the insurer must respond by` (`d` 16 7 2025)
-- No response by then: on 17 July it is conclusively presumed satisfied (s 39(3)).
#ASSERT `Is the insurer taken to accept my notice` (`d` 2 7 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 17 7 2025) EQUALS `the insurer is conclusively presumed satisfied that the notice was given as required (s 39(3))` (`d` 16 7 2025)
-- A response on the last day is in time; one on 17 July is too late to stop the presumption.
#ASSERT `Is the insurer taken to accept my notice` (`d` 2 7 2025) TRUE (`d` 16 7 2025) (`d` 20 7 2025) EQUALS `the insurer responded in time; what follows depends on its response (s 39(1))`
#ASSERT `Is the insurer taken to accept my notice` (`d` 2 7 2025) TRUE (`d` 17 7 2025) (`d` 20 7 2025) EQUALS `the insurer is conclusively presumed satisfied that the notice was given as required (s 39(3))` (`d` 16 7 2025)
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 39 -- the insurer must respond to the notice of claim within 14 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `give written notice responding to the notice of claim` 14)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the insurer, "s 39(3): the insurer did not respond within 14 days ... conclusively presumed satisfied ..." (response on day 15)
#TRACE `s 39 -- the insurer must respond to the notice of claim within 14 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `give written notice responding to the notice of claim` AT 15

-- s 39(5): a compliant notice: he may proceed. A late notice: he may proceed only if the insurer is satisfied, is
-- presumed satisfied, waives, or the court allows it; otherwise not.
#ASSERT `Can I go on with my claim` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claimant may proceed further with the claim`
#ASSERT `Can I go on with my claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claimant may not proceed further: notice was not given as required, and none of s 39(5)(a) to (c) applies`
#ASSERT `Can I go on with my claim` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claimant may proceed further with the claim`
#ASSERT `Can I go on with my claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the claimant may proceed further with the claim`
#ASSERT `Can I go on with my claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the claimant may proceed further with the claim`
#ASSERT `Can I go on with my claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the claimant may proceed further with the claim`

-- s 41(1): received as required on 2 July 2025: liability notice due by 2 January 2026. Day count for the rule:
-- 29 (rest of July) + 31 + 30 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 2 = 184.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer say whether it admits liability` TRUE (`d` 2 7 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `the insurer must say whether it admits or denies liability by` (`d` 2 1 2026)
#ASSERT `the days in` 6 `months from` (`d` 2 7 2025) EQUALS 184
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 41 -- the insurer must say whether it admits or denies liability within 6 months` 184) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `give written notice admitting or denying liability` 184)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the insurer, "s 41(1): ... not ... within 6 months ..." (notice on day 185)
#TRACE `s 41 -- the insurer must say whether it admits or denies liability within 6 months` 184 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the insurer` DOES `give written notice admitting or denying liability` AT 185
-- s 41(3): a notice that did not comply, waived on 10 September 2025: 6 months from then, 10 March 2026. No waiver,
-- satisfaction or court order yet: the 6 months have not started. Received 31 August 2025 as required: 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer say whether it admits liability` FALSE (`d` 2 7 2025) TRUE (`d` 10 9 2025) EQUALS `the insurer must say whether it admits or denies liability by` (`d` 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer say whether it admits liability` FALSE (`d` 2 7 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `the 6 months have not started: the notice is not yet taken to be received (s 41(3))`
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer say whether it admits liability` TRUE (`d` 31 8 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `the insurer must say whether it admits or denies liability by` (`d` 28 2 2026)

-- s 37A(3): additional information requested 15 May 2025: by 15 June 2025 (31 days). Requested 31 January 2025: by
-- 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I give the additional information form` (`d` 15 5 2025) EQUALS `d` 15 6 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I give the additional information form` (`d` 31 1 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `the days in` 1 `months from` (`d` 15 5 2025) EQUALS 31
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 37A -- the claimant must give the additional information form within 1 month after the request` 31) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `give the additional information form` 31)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the claimant, "s 37A(3): the additional information form was not given within 1 month ..." (day 32)
#TRACE `s 37A -- the claimant must give the additional information form within 1 month after the request` 31 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `give the additional information form` AT 32

-- s 45: notice given 20 June 2025: his reports and documents by 20 July 2025. A request received 31 October 2025:
-- answer by 30 November 2025 (30 days). A change he learns of on 5 January 2026: tell the insurer by 5 February 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I give the insurer documents or information` `give copies of reports and documents I hold when I give notice` (`d` 20 6 2025) EQUALS `d` 20 7 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I give the insurer documents or information` `answer the insurer's request for information` (`d` 31 10 2025) EQUALS `d` 30 11 2025
#ASSERT `By when must I give the insurer documents or information` `tell the insurer of a significant change in my condition or circumstances` (`d` 5 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 5 2 2026
#ASSERT `the days in` 1 `months from` (`d` 31 10 2025) EQUALS 30
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 45 -- the claimant must respond to the insurer's request for information within 1 month` 30) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `respond to the request for information` 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the claimant, "s 45(2)(b): ... within 1 month ..." (day 31)
#TRACE `s 45 -- the claimant must respond to the insurer's request for information within 1 month` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `respond to the request for information` AT 31
-- s 47: the insurer received notice on 23 June 2025: its reports by 23 July 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must the insurer give me its reports or information` (`d` 23 6 2025) EQUALS `d` 23 7 2025

-- s 42: liability admitted, $10,000 of expenses, 20% contributory negligence asserted: 10,000 x 0.8 = 8,000.
#ASSERT `How much of my medical expenses must the insurer pay` TRUE 10000 20 FALSE EQUALS `the insurer must pay, in Australian dollars,` 8000
#ASSERT `How much of my medical expenses must the insurer pay` TRUE 10000 0 FALSE EQUALS `the insurer must pay, in Australian dollars,` 10000
#ASSERT `How much of my medical expenses must the insurer pay` FALSE 10000 20 FALSE EQUALS `no duty yet: liability has not been admitted (s 42(1))`
#ASSERT `How much of my medical expenses must the insurer pay` TRUE 10000 20 TRUE EQUALS `the insurer need not pay for treatment, care and support needs (s 42(3))`

-- s 41(5): an offer received 15 January 2026: respond by 15 April 2026 (16 + 28 + 31 + 15 = 90 days). One received
-- 30 November 2025: 30 February does not exist, so 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I respond to a settlement offer` (`d` 15 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 15 4 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I respond to a settlement offer` (`d` 30 11 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `the days in` 3 `months from` (`d` 15 1 2026) EQUALS 90
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 41(5) -- the claimant must respond to a written offer of settlement within 3 months` 90) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `respond in writing to the offer` 90)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the claimant, "s 41(5): no written response ... within 3 months ..." (day 91)
#TRACE `s 41(5) -- the claimant must respond to a written offer of settlement within 3 months` 90 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `respond in writing to the offer` AT 91

-- s 51(9A), the Act's own example: 50% apportionment, damages $20,000 before rehabilitation, $5,000 spent:
-- (20,000 + 5,000) x 0.5 = 12,500; less 5,000 = 7,500.
#ASSERT `How does rehabilitation affect my damages` 20000 5000 50 TRUE EQUALS 7500
-- No s 51(4) statement: the cost is not taken into account (s 51(9)): 20,000 x 0.5 = 10,000.
#ASSERT `How does rehabilitation affect my damages` 20000 5000 50 FALSE EQUALS 10000
-- No contributory negligence: 25,000 - 5,000 = 20,000.
#ASSERT `How does rehabilitation affect my damages` 20000 5000 0 TRUE EQUALS 20000
-- Finding 7: rehabilitation costing more than the reduced damages: (2,000 + 10,000) x 0.5 - 10,000 = -4,000. The
-- text gives no floor.
#ASSERT `How does rehabilitation affect my damages` 2000 10000 50 TRUE EQUALS -4000

-- s 51A(3): notice given 20 June 2025, no additional information: relevant date 20 December 2025; he may nominate a
-- time and place once it has passed, from 21 December 2025.
#ASSERT `From when can I call the compulsory conference` (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `I may call the conference at a reasonable time and place I nominate from` (`d` 21 12 2025)
-- Additional information form given 10 December 2025: 1 month later, 10 January 2026, is later: from 11 January 2026.
#ASSERT `From when can I call the compulsory conference` (`d` 20 6 2025) TRUE (`d` 10 12 2025) EQUALS `I may call the conference at a reasonable time and place I nominate from` (`d` 11 1 2026)
-- Form given 1 August 2025: 1 September 2025 is earlier than 20 December 2025: from 21 December 2025.
#ASSERT `From when can I call the compulsory conference` (`d` 20 6 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 8 2025) EQUALS `I may call the conference at a reasonable time and place I nominate from` (`d` 21 12 2025)

-- s 51B(5): conference on 15 April 2026: documents by 8 April 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I exchange documents before the conference` (`d` 15 4 2026) EQUALS `d` 8 4 2026
-- s 51C(1)(b): conference dispensed with on 20 January 2026: offers by 3 February 2026 (20 + 14 = 34 January).
#ASSERT `By when must final offers be exchanged` (`d` 20 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 3 2 2026
-- s 51C(6): offers exchanged at the conference on 15 April 2026 stay open 14 days, to 29 April; proceedings from
-- 30 April 2026.
#ASSERT `the first day proceedings may be started after the offers (s 51C(6))` (`d` 15 4 2026) EQUALS `d` 30 4 2026
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 51C(6) -- the claimant must not start proceedings while a mandatory final offer remains open` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `give written notice admitting or denying liability` 15)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `s 51C(6) -- the claimant must not start proceedings while a mandatory final offer remains open` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `start proceedings` 15)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the claimant, "s 51C(6): proceedings must not be started while a mandatory final offer remains open" (day 14)
#TRACE `s 51C(6) -- the claimant must not start proceedings while a mandatory final offer remains open` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `start proceedings` AT 14

-- s 51D(1): conference concluded 15 April 2026: start by 14 June 2026 (15 + 31 + 14 = 60 days).
#ASSERT `By when should I start my court action` FALSE (`d` 15 4 2026) (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `the action should be started by` (`d` 14 6 2026)
-- A further period agreed within the 60 days, to 31 July 2026.
#ASSERT `By when should I start my court action` FALSE (`d` 15 4 2026) (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 31 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS `the action should be started by` (`d` 31 7 2026)
-- s 51D(3): the court dispensed with mandatory final offers.
#ASSERT `By when should I start my court action` FALSE (`d` 15 4 2026) (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE EQUALS `the action should be started within the period the court fixed when dispensing with mandatory final offers (s 51D(3))`
-- s 51D(2): conference dispensed with on 20 January 2026; 6 months after notice is 20 December 2025; the later is
-- 20 January 2026; + 60 days: 11 (to 31 January) + 28 + 21 = 21 March 2026.
#ASSERT `By when should I start my court action` TRUE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 20 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `the action should be started by` (`d` 21 3 2026)
-- Finding 9, s 51D(2)(a)(i) as written: additional information given 10 December 2025, dispensed with 1 December 2025:
-- the later is 10 December 2025; + 60 days: 21 + 31 + 8 = 8 February 2026.
#ASSERT `By when should I start my court action` TRUE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 20 6 2025) TRUE (`d` 10 12 2025) (`d` 1 12 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `the action should be started by` (`d` 8 2 2026)

-- s 51D(4)-(5): the court fixed 30 September 2026 as the time limit.
#ASSERT `Is my claim barred for not starting in time` TRUE (`d` 30 9 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 30 9 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my claim barred for not starting in time` TRUE (`d` 30 9 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 10 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my claim barred for not starting in time` TRUE (`d` 30 9 2026) TRUE (`d` 30 9 2026) (`d` 5 10 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my claim barred for not starting in time` TRUE (`d` 30 9 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 5 10 2026) EQUALS TRUE
-- No time limit fixed: the 60 days' expiry does not bar (s 51D(4)).
#ASSERT `Is my claim barred for not starting in time` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 5 10 2027) EQUALS FALSE
-- The s 51D rule: day 0 the conference concluded; started on day 60, in time.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 51D -- the claimant should start the action within 60 days, and must within any limit the court fixes` 60 TRUE 30) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `start proceedings` 60)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- The 60 days pass (an insurer's event on day 61); the court's 30-day limit runs from then, to day 91: started on 91.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 51D -- the claimant should start the action within 60 days, and must within any limit the court fixes` 60 TRUE 30) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `give written notice admitting or denying liability` 61), (EVENT `the claimant` `start proceedings` 91)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- No time limit fixed: starting on day 400 is still allowed.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 51D -- the claimant should start the action within 60 days, and must within any limit the court fixes` 60 FALSE 0) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `give written notice admitting or denying liability` 61), (EVENT `the claimant` `start proceedings` 400)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the claimant, "s 51D(5): the action was not started within the time limit the court fixed ... barred" (started day 92)
#TRACE `s 51D -- the claimant should start the action within 60 days, and must within any limit the court fixes` 60 TRUE 30 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 61)
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `start proceedings` AT 92

-- s 52: the insured driver is known and alive: both, jointly. Unidentified or dead: the insurer alone may be sued.
#ASSERT `Whom do I sue` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `against the insured person and the insurer as joint defendants (s 52(1))`
#ASSERT `Whom do I sue` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `against the insurer alone, or the insured person and the insurer jointly (s 52(2))`
#ASSERT `Whom do I sue` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `against the insurer alone, or the insured person and the insurer jointly (s 52(2))`

-- s 57: Sam's period of limitation (HYPOTHETICAL: 3 years) ends 10 March 2028. s 57(3): the last 14 days run from
-- 26 February 2028 (10 March less 13 days: 10 days back to 29 February in a leap year, 3 more) to 10 March 2028.
#ASSERT `Can I give notice to the commission` (`d` 10 3 2028) (`d` 26 2 2028) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I give notice to the commission` (`d` 10 3 2028) (`d` 10 3 2028) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I give notice to the commission` (`d` 10 3 2028) (`d` 25 2 2028) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I give notice to the commission` (`d` 10 3 2028) (`d` 11 3 2028) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I give notice to the commission` (`d` 10 3 2028) (`d` 1 3 2028) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 57(1)-(2): notice given 1 March 2028, before the end: proceedings up to 1 September 2028.
#ASSERT `Can I bring proceedings after the limitation period` (`d` 10 3 2028) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2028) FALSE (`d` 1 9 2028) EQUALS `s 57 lets proceedings be brought after the period of limitation, up to and including` (`d` 1 9 2028)
#ASSERT `Can I bring proceedings after the limitation period` (`d` 10 3 2028) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2028) FALSE (`d` 2 9 2028) EQUALS `s 57 does not help: the 6 months after notice have ended and the court has allowed no longer period`
#ASSERT `Can I bring proceedings after the limitation period` (`d` 10 3 2028) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2028) TRUE (`d` 2 9 2028) EQUALS `s 57 lets proceedings be brought within the longer period the court allows (s 57(2)(b))`
-- Notice on the last day of the period counts; given the day after, it does not.
#ASSERT `Can I bring proceedings after the limitation period` (`d` 10 3 2028) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2028) FALSE (`d` 10 9 2028) EQUALS `s 57 lets proceedings be brought after the period of limitation, up to and including` (`d` 10 9 2028)
#ASSERT `Can I bring proceedings after the limitation period` (`d` 10 3 2028) TRUE (`d` 11 3 2028) FALSE (`d` 1 4 2028) EQUALS `s 57 does not help: notice was not given before the period of limitation ended`
#ASSERT `Can I bring proceedings after the limitation period` (`d` 10 3 2028) TRUE (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE (`d` 10 3 2028) EQUALS `the period of limitation has not ended`

-- Can Sam start on a given day? Base facts: notice 20 June 2025 as required; conference held; offers exchanged
-- 15 April 2026; no court time limit; limitation ends 10 March 2028. On 1 May 2026: nothing stops him.
#ASSERT `Can I start my court action on this day` TRUE (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 4 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 10 3 2028) FALSE (`d` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `nothing in the Act stops me starting my court action on this day`
#ASSERT `Can I start my court action on this day` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 10 3 2028) FALSE (`d` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `not yet: I must first give notice of the claim to the insurer (s 37(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I start my court action on this day` TRUE (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 4 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 10 3 2028) FALSE (`d` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `no: my notice was not given as required and neither the insurer nor the court has accepted it (s 39(5))`
#ASSERT `Can I start my court action on this day` TRUE (`d` 20 6 2025) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 4 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 10 3 2028) FALSE (`d` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `no: the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred (ss 37(3), 39(8))`
#ASSERT `Can I start my court action on this day` TRUE (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 10 3 2028) FALSE (`d` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `not yet: there must first be a compulsory conference, unless it is dispensed with (s 51A(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I start my court action on this day` TRUE (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 10 3 2028) FALSE (`d` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `not yet: mandatory final offers must first be exchanged (s 51C(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I start my court action on this day` TRUE (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 10 3 2028) FALSE (`d` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `nothing in the Act stops me starting my court action on this day`
-- The offers stay open to 29 April 2026: on that day not yet; from 30 April he may.
#ASSERT `Can I start my court action on this day` TRUE (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 4 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 10 3 2028) FALSE (`d` 29 4 2026) EQUALS `not yet: a mandatory final offer is still open; I may start from` (`d` 30 4 2026)
#ASSERT `Can I start my court action on this day` TRUE (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 4 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 10 3 2028) FALSE (`d` 30 4 2026) EQUALS `nothing in the Act stops me starting my court action on this day`
-- A court time limit of 30 September 2026: on 1 October 2026 the claim is barred.
#ASSERT `Can I start my court action on this day` TRUE (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 4 2026) TRUE (`d` 30 9 2026) (`d` 10 3 2028) FALSE (`d` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `no: the claim is barred because I did not start within the time limit the court fixed (s 51D(5))`
#ASSERT `Can I start my court action on this day` TRUE (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 4 2026) TRUE (`d` 30 9 2026) (`d` 10 3 2028) FALSE (`d` 30 9 2026) EQUALS `nothing in the Act stops me starting my court action on this day`
-- Finding 11: on 11 March 2028, after the period of limitation, notice in June 2025 does not help: its 6 months ended
-- 20 December 2025. With a longer period from the court, it does.
#ASSERT `Can I start my court action on this day` TRUE (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 4 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 10 3 2028) FALSE (`d` 11 3 2028) EQUALS `no: the period of limitation has ended and s 57 does not extend it`
#ASSERT `Can I start my court action on this day` TRUE (`d` 20 6 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 4 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 10 3 2028) TRUE (`d` 11 3 2028) EQUALS `nothing in the Act stops me starting my court action on this day`

-- s 55F, with HYPOTHETICAL limits: lower $50,000, upper $100,000.
-- (2)(a): award $40,000 between the claimant's $60,000 and the insurer's $30,000: no costs. And at the lower limit.
#ASSERT `Who gets costs on a small award` 40000 60000 30000 50000 100000 EQUALS `no costs are to be awarded (s 55F(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Who gets costs on a small award` 50000 60000 30000 50000 100000 EQUALS `no costs are to be awarded (s 55F(2)(a))`
-- (2)(b): award $50,000, claimant offered $45,000. (2)(c): award $30,000, equal to the insurer's $30,000.
#ASSERT `Who gets costs on a small award` 50000 45000 30000 50000 100000 EQUALS `costs to the claimant on an indemnity basis from the day proceedings started, none before (s 55F(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Who gets costs on a small award` 30000 60000 30000 50000 100000 EQUALS `costs to the insurer on a standard basis from the day proceedings started, none before (s 55F(2)(c))`
-- (3)(a): $50,001, just over the lower limit, between the offers.
#ASSERT `Who gets costs on a small award` 50001 60000 30000 50000 100000 EQUALS `costs to the claimant on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit (s 55F(3)(a))`
-- (3)(b): equal to the claimant's offer; and at the upper limit itself.
#ASSERT `Who gets costs on a small award` 60000 60000 30000 50000 100000 EQUALS `costs to the claimant on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit before proceedings started, and on an indemnity basis after (s 55F(3)(b))`
#ASSERT `Who gets costs on a small award` 100000 60000 30000 50000 100000 EQUALS `costs to the claimant on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit before proceedings started, and on an indemnity basis after (s 55F(3)(b))`
-- (3)(c): $70,000 at or below the insurer's $80,000, claimant offered $120,000.
#ASSERT `Who gets costs on a small award` 70000 120000 80000 50000 100000 EQUALS `costs to the claimant on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit before proceedings started; to the insurer on a standard basis after (s 55F(3)(c))`
-- Just over the upper limit: s 55F does not apply.
#ASSERT `Who gets costs on a small award` 100001 60000 30000 50000 100000 EQUALS `s 55F does not apply: the award is more than the upper offer limit`
-- Finding 10: the claimant offered $40,000 and the insurer $70,000; $60,000 meets both (b) and (c); (b) is taken.
#ASSERT `Who gets costs on a small award` 60000 40000 70000 50000 100000 EQUALS `costs to the claimant on a standard basis up to the declared costs limit before proceedings started, and on an indemnity basis after (s 55F(3)(b))`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 2. Priya is hit by a car that drives off, in Cairns, on 15 January 2025. It is never identified: her claim is
-- against the Nominal Defendant.
-- =====================================================================================================================
-- s 37(2)(a): within 3 months, by 15 April 2025. On 16 April, not given: late.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 15 4 2025) EQUALS `notice of the claim must be given by` (`d` 15 4 2025)
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 16 4 2025) EQUALS `notice is late: it must still be given, with a reasonable excuse for the delay (s 37(3))` (`d` 15 4 2025)
-- A lawyer consulted does not matter for an unidentified vehicle: still 15 April 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) TRUE (`d` 20 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 2 2025) EQUALS `notice of the claim must be given by` (`d` 15 4 2025)
-- s 37(3): 9 months end 15 October 2025. Not given by 15 October: late but not barred; on 16 October: barred.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 15 10 2025) EQUALS `notice is late: it must still be given, with a reasonable excuse for the delay (s 37(3))` (`d` 15 4 2025)
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 16 10 2025) EQUALS `the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred: no notice within 9 months (ss 37(3), 39(8))` (`d` 15 10 2025)
-- Given on 15 October 2025, asked later: late, not barred. Given on 16 October: barred.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 15 10 2025) (`d` 1 11 2025) EQUALS `notice is late: it must still be given, with a reasonable excuse for the delay (s 37(3))` (`d` 15 4 2025)
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 1 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 16 10 2025) (`d` 1 11 2025) EQUALS `the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred: no notice within 9 months (ss 37(3), 39(8))` (`d` 15 10 2025)
-- s 39(5), (8): once barred, nothing the Nominal Defendant or a court does lets her go on.
#ASSERT `Can I go on with my claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the claimant may not proceed: the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred, and it cannot waive nor the court give leave (ss 37(3), 39(8))`

-- The s 37 rule for Priya. Day 0 is 15 January 2025; 15 April 2025 is 16 + 28 + 31 + 15 = day 90; 15 October 2025 is
-- day 273 (16 + 28 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 31 + 30 + 15). The second window runs from day 91: 273 - 90 - 1 = 182.
#ASSERT `the days in the s 37(2) period for` (`Notice facts` WITH `the day of the accident` IS `d` 15 1 2025, `the vehicle can be identified` IS FALSE, `symptoms were immediately apparent` IS TRUE, `the day symptoms first appeared` IS `d` 15 1 2025, `a lawyer has been consulted about a possible claim` IS FALSE, `the day a lawyer was first consulted` IS `d` 1 1 2000, `the obligation was suspended by minority or incapacity` IS FALSE, `the day the minority or incapacity ended` IS `d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS 90
#ASSERT `the days after the s 37(2) period to the bar for` (`Notice facts` WITH `the day of the accident` IS `d` 15 1 2025, `the vehicle can be identified` IS FALSE, `symptoms were immediately apparent` IS TRUE, `the day symptoms first appeared` IS `d` 15 1 2025, `a lawyer has been consulted about a possible claim` IS FALSE, `the day a lawyer was first consulted` IS `d` 1 1 2000, `the obligation was suspended by minority or incapacity` IS FALSE, `the day the minority or incapacity ended` IS `d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS 182
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 37 -- the claimant must give notice of the claim within the period, and after it with a reasonable excuse` 90 FALSE 182) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `give notice of the claim` 90)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Late on the last day of the 9 months (day 273 = 91 + 182): the continuing obligation is met.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 37 -- the claimant must give notice of the claim within the period, and after it with a reasonable excuse` 90 FALSE 182) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the insurer` `give written notice responding to the notice of claim` 91), (EVENT `the claimant` `give notice of the claim with a reasonable excuse for the delay` 273)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the claimant, "s 37(3): notice was not given to the Nominal Defendant within 9 months ... barred" (notice on day 274)
#TRACE `s 37 -- the claimant must give notice of the claim within the period, and after it with a reasonable excuse` 90 FALSE 182 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 91)
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `give notice of the claim with a reasonable excuse for the delay` AT 274

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 3. Leo is 17 when injured as a passenger on 1 February 2024; he turns 18 on 1 September 2024. His parents
-- consult a lawyer on 1 March 2024. Symptoms are immediate.
-- =====================================================================================================================
-- s 40 (finding 2): the periods begin on 1 September 2024. 9 months: 1 June 2025; 1 month after the later of the
-- lawyer and 1 September 2024: 1 October 2024. The earlier: 1 October 2024.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 1 2 2024) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 10 2024) EQUALS `notice of the claim must be given by` (`d` 1 10 2024)
-- Without s 40 the same facts would give 1 April 2024 (1 month after the lawyer).
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 1 2 2024) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 3 2024) EQUALS `notice of the claim must be given by` (`d` 1 4 2024)
-- s 40(3): notice given for him on 15 March 2024, during his minority: in time.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 1 2 2024) TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2024) TRUE (`d` 1 9 2024) TRUE (`d` 15 3 2024) (`d` 1 10 2024) EQUALS `notice was given within the s 37(2) period`
-- Had the vehicle been unidentified: 3 months from 1 September 2024, 1 December 2024; barred only after 1 June 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 1 2 2024) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 11 2024) EQUALS `notice of the claim must be given by` (`d` 1 12 2024)
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 1 2 2024) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 6 2025) EQUALS `notice is late: it must still be given, with a reasonable excuse for the delay (s 37(3))` (`d` 1 12 2024)
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my claim` (`d` 1 2 2024) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 1 9 2024) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 2 6 2025) EQUALS `the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred: no notice within 9 months (ss 37(3), 39(8))` (`d` 1 6 2025)
